industries to the Chinese hinterland and the rest of Asia paved the way for the growth
of producer services in Hong Kong.
Hong Kong’s relocation of manufacturing industries into mainland China was
associated with significant investment flows, which then created a demand for China
related trade activities in Hong Kong and gave impetus to the growth of Hong Kong’s
reexports. Indeed, Figure 4 shows the close relationship between the annual growth
